{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-reviews
  Section 7 - cream cards on a peach section background showing three
  featured reviews. Aggregate rating row in the heading bar, locked
  decisions:
    - count == 0: aggregate hidden (pre-launch state)
    - 0 < count < threshold: stars only, no number (honest > inflated)
    - count >= threshold: full "X.X - N reviews"
  Manual settings drive the aggregate by default; the use_judgeme_widget
  toggle swaps in Judge.me's JS-hydrated all-reviews widget once the
  number flow is worth automating.

  One kid character (random-of-three) anchored to the top-right of the
  middle card with the same scroll-pop pattern as theinmag-mission and
  theinmag-philosophy. Hidden below 750px - phones are too tight.

  Photo OR video per review (video wins when both are set). Cards
  without media still render, just quieter. Video uses native controls,
  muted by default - visitor presses play.

  Cream cards are uniform per the locked palette decision (B). Variation
  shows through media presence and per-card content, not background
  colour.

  No aggregateRating / Review JSON-LD on this section by design - Google
  reserves both for single-item pages and Search Console flags them on
  homepage/category pages. Judge.me handles review schema correctly on
  the product pages where it earns rich results.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign heading = section.settings.heading
  assign subhead = section.settings.subhead
  assign cta_label = section.settings.cta_label
  assign cta_link = section.settings.cta_link
  assign show_cta = section.settings.show_cta

  assign use_judgeme = section.settings.use_judgeme_widget
  assign aggregate_rating = section.settings.aggregate_rating | default: 5
  assign review_count = section.settings.review_count | default: 0
  assign threshold = section.settings.show_count_threshold | default: 100

  assign jm = shop.metafields.judgeme
  assign jm_carousel = jm.featured_carousel
  assign judgeme_card_count = section.settings.judgeme_card_count | default: 4
  assign show_judgeme_cards = false
  if section.settings.use_judgeme_cards and jm_carousel != blank
    assign show_judgeme_cards = true
  endif

  comment
    Review-invite bridge. Judge.me's hosted store-review form sends
    x-frame-options: SAMEORIGIN, so it can't be iframed into a lightbox
    on our domain. Instead the invite opens a branded modal whose stars
    deep-link to the same store-review URL the Klaviyo blast uses, with
    the tapped rating pre-filled. Matches the locked store-review model
    (klaviyo-review-request-flow.md), not a product-scoped on-site form.
  endcomment
  assign show_review_invite = section.settings.show_review_invite
  assign store_review_link = section.settings.store_review_link | default: 'https://judge.me/product_reviews/428871d8-caf3-42ff-96f7-22ca4a1d9976/new?store-review-only=true&source=shareable-link'
  assign invite_heading = section.settings.invite_heading
  assign invite_text = section.settings.invite_text
  assign invite_cta = section.settings.invite_cta
  assign rmodal_title = section.settings.rmodal_title
  assign rmodal_body = section.settings.rmodal_body
  assign rmodal_cta = section.settings.rmodal_cta
  assign rmodal_note = section.settings.rmodal_note

  assign bg_src = ''
  if section.settings.background_image != blank
    assign bg_src = section.settings.background_image | image_url: width: 2400
  elsif section.settings.background_filename != blank
    assign bg_src = section.settings.background_filename | asset_url
  endif

  assign section_class = 'theinmag-reviews'
  if bg_src != blank
    assign section_class = 'theinmag-reviews theinmag-reviews--has-bg'
  endif

  assign section_style = '--reviews-pt: ' | append: section.settings.padding_top | append: 'px; --reviews-pb: ' | append: section.settings.padding_bottom | append: 'px;'
  if bg_src != blank
    assign section_style = section_style | append: " --reviews-bg: url('" | append: bg_src | append: "');"
  endif

  comment
    Anchor the character to the middle card. Falls back gracefully when
    the section ships with fewer than three blocks.
  endcomment
  assign middle_index = 2
  if section.blocks.size < 3
    assign middle_index = 1
  endif

  assign rating_x10 = aggregate_rating | times: 10 | round
-%}

<section
  class="{{ section_class }}"
  data-theinmag-reviews
  aria-labelledby="theinmag-reviews-heading"
  style="{{ section_style }}"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    Decorative dots pattern behind everything. Rotated 90° and
    oversized so the dot trail spans edge-to-edge across the desktop
    viewport, breaking up the flat lavender. Sits at the lowest
    stacking layer; pointer-events:none so it doesn't intercept
    clicks. aria-hidden because it's purely decorative.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <img
    class="theinmag-reviews__dots"
    src="{{ 'dotsforbehindtam.png' | asset_url }}"
    alt=""
    aria-hidden="true"
    loading="lazy"
  >

  {% render 'theinmag-character-pool' %}
  <span class="theinmag-reviews__character" data-theinmag-pool-character></span>

  <div class="theinmag-reviews__inner">
    <header class="theinmag-reviews__header">
      <div class="theinmag-reviews__title-stack">
        {%- if heading != blank -%}
          <h2 id="theinmag-reviews-heading" class="theinmag-reviews__heading">{{ heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if subhead != blank -%}
          <p class="theinmag-reviews__subhead">{{ subhead }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if review_count > 0 or use_judgeme -%}
        <div class="theinmag-reviews__aggregate">
          {%- if use_judgeme -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Judge.me's App Embed JS hydrates these placeholder elements
              after page load. The wrapper class hides them visually
              until JS injects the rating + count, preventing flash.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="theinmag-reviews__aggregate-jdgm">
              <div class="jdgm-all-reviews-rating" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <span class="jdgm-all-reviews-count" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </div>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="theinmag-reviews__stars" role="img" aria-label="{{ aggregate_rating }} out of 5 stars">
              {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
                {%- assign full_at = i | times: 10 -%}
                {%- assign prev_at = i | minus: 1 | times: 10 -%}
                {%- assign fill_pct = 0 -%}
                {%- if rating_x10 >= full_at -%}
                  {%- assign fill_pct = 100 -%}
                {%- elsif rating_x10 > prev_at -%}
                  {%- assign fill_pct = rating_x10 | minus: prev_at | times: 10 -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="theinmag-reviews__star" style="--fill: {{ fill_pct }}%"></span>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </span>
            {%- if review_count >= threshold -%}
              <span class="theinmag-reviews__aggregate-text">
                <span class="theinmag-reviews__aggregate-value">{{ aggregate_rating }}</span>
                <span class="theinmag-reviews__aggregate-sep" aria-hidden="true"> - </span>
                <span class="theinmag-reviews__aggregate-count">{{ review_count }} reviews</span>
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>

    {%- if show_review_invite and store_review_link != blank -%}
      <div class="theinmag-reviews__invite">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="theinmag-reviews__invite-card"
          data-theinmag-rmodal-open
          aria-haspopup="dialog"
        >
          <span class="theinmag-reviews__invite-stars" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- for i in (1..5) -%}<span class="theinmag-reviews__star" style="--fill: 100%"></span>{%- endfor -%}
          </span>
          <span class="theinmag-reviews__invite-copy">
            {%- if invite_heading != blank -%}<span class="theinmag-reviews__invite-heading">{{ invite_heading }}</span>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if invite_text != blank -%}<span class="theinmag-reviews__invite-text">{{ invite_text }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          </span>
          <span class="theinmag-reviews__invite-cta">{{ invite_cta | default: 'Write a review' }}</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_judgeme_cards -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Judge.me masonry. shop.metafields.judgeme.featured_carousel renders
        Judge.me's carousel markup server-side; the script block below
        reparents the .jdgm-carousel-item nodes into this grid (so CSS
        columns can lay them out), caps to judgeme_card_count, and strips
        the carousel chrome. Falls back to the manual blocks below when the
        metafield is blank (e.g. before any reviews are featured).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div
        class="theinmag-reviews__jdgm"
        data-theinmag-reviews-jdgm
        data-card-cap="{{ judgeme_card_count }}"
      >
        <div class="theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid" data-theinmag-reviews-jdgm-host>
          {{ jm_carousel }}
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- if show_cta and cta_label != blank and cta_link != blank -%}
        <div class="theinmag-reviews__cta-wrap theinmag-reviews__cta-wrap--jdgm">
          <a class="theinmag-reviews__cta" href="{{ cta_link }}">{{ cta_label }}</a>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- elsif section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Fallback (no Judge.me data): two-column on desktop. Left = stack of
        text-only review cards. Right = single video review card (video frame
        on top, written review below). Mobile: video card first, then
        text stack.

        Reviews are split by whether video_url is set. Multiple videos:
        only the first renders as the "right" card; any extras fall
        through to the text stack (rare edge case for the homepage).

        Photo display is intentionally dropped from the homepage
        rendering - the schema field stays for use on /pages/reviews
        later. Homepage cards are either video (right) or pure text
        (left stack), no avatar treatment, for visual uniformity.
      {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- liquid
        assign video_block_index = 0
        for block in section.blocks
          if block.settings.video_url != blank and video_block_index == 0
            assign video_block_index = forloop.index
          endif
        endfor
      -%}

      <div class="theinmag-reviews__layout">

        {%- comment -%} Left column: stacked text-only review cards. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="theinmag-reviews__text-stack" role="list">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.settings.video_url == blank or forloop.index != video_block_index -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign rating = block.settings.rating | default: 5
                assign body = block.settings.body
                assign reviewer_name = block.settings.name
                assign reviewer_location = block.settings.location
              -%}
              <article class="theinmag-reviews__card theinmag-reviews__card--text" role="listitem" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <div class="theinmag-reviews__card-stars" role="img" aria-label="{{ rating }} out of 5 stars">
                  {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
                    {%- assign fill_pct = 0 -%}
                    {%- if i <= rating -%}{%- assign fill_pct = 100 -%}{%- endif -%}
                    <span class="theinmag-reviews__star" style="--fill: {{ fill_pct }}%"></span>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>

                {%- if body != blank -%}
                  <p class="theinmag-reviews__card-body">{{ body }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if reviewer_name != blank or reviewer_location != blank -%}
                  <p class="theinmag-reviews__card-attribution">
                    {%- if reviewer_name != blank -%}
                      <span class="theinmag-reviews__card-name">{{ reviewer_name }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {%- if reviewer_location != blank -%}
                      <span class="theinmag-reviews__card-location">{{ reviewer_location }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </article>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}

          {%- if show_cta and cta_label != blank and cta_link != blank -%}
            <div class="theinmag-reviews__cta-wrap">
              <a class="theinmag-reviews__cta" href="{{ cta_link }}">{{ cta_label }}</a>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Right column: single video review card. Video frame at 1:1,
          then the written review below.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if video_block_index > 0 -%}
          {%- assign video_index_zero = video_block_index | minus: 1 -%}
          {%- assign video_block = section.blocks[video_index_zero] -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign v_rating = video_block.settings.rating | default: 5
            assign v_body = video_block.settings.body
            assign v_name = video_block.settings.name
            assign v_location = video_block.settings.location
            assign v_video = video_block.settings.video_url
            assign v_poster = ''
            if video_block.settings.photo != blank
              assign v_poster = video_block.settings.photo | image_url: width: 1200
            elsif video_block.settings.photo_filename != blank
              assign v_poster = video_block.settings.photo_filename | asset_url
            endif
          -%}
          <div class="theinmag-reviews__video-column">
            <article class="theinmag-reviews__card theinmag-reviews__card--video" {{ video_block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <div class="theinmag-reviews__card-video">
                <video
                  src="{{ v_video }}"
                  controls
                  muted
                  playsinline
                  preload="metadata"
                  {%- if v_poster != blank %} poster="{{ v_poster }}"{% endif -%}
                ></video>
              </div>

              <div class="theinmag-reviews__card-video-body">
                <div class="theinmag-reviews__card-stars" role="img" aria-label="{{ v_rating }} out of 5 stars">
                  {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
                    {%- assign fill_pct = 0 -%}
                    {%- if i <= v_rating -%}{%- assign fill_pct = 100 -%}{%- endif -%}
                    <span class="theinmag-reviews__star" style="--fill: {{ fill_pct }}%"></span>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>

                {%- if v_body != blank -%}
                  <p class="theinmag-reviews__card-body">{{ v_body }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if v_name != blank or v_location != blank -%}
                  <p class="theinmag-reviews__card-attribution">
                    {%- if v_name != blank -%}<span class="theinmag-reviews__card-name">{{ v_name }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                    {%- if v_location != blank -%}<span class="theinmag-reviews__card-location">{{ v_location }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                  </p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if show_review_invite and store_review_link != blank -%}
    <div
      class="theinmag-reviews__rmodal"
      data-theinmag-rmodal
      data-store-review-link="{{ store_review_link | escape }}"
      hidden
      aria-hidden="true"
      role="dialog"
      aria-modal="true"
      aria-labelledby="theinmag-rmodal-title"
    >
      <div class="theinmag-reviews__rmodal-backdrop" data-theinmag-rmodal-close></div>

      <div class="theinmag-reviews__rmodal-panel" role="document">
        <button
          class="theinmag-reviews__rmodal-x"
          type="button"
          aria-label="Close"
          data-theinmag-rmodal-close
        >
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <line x1="4" y1="4" x2="16" y2="16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <line x1="16" y1="4" x2="4" y2="16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <h2 id="theinmag-rmodal-title" class="theinmag-reviews__rmodal-title">{{ rmodal_title | default: 'Did theINmag spark something?' }}</h2>
        {%- if rmodal_body != blank -%}
          <p class="theinmag-reviews__rmodal-body">{{ rmodal_body }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="theinmag-reviews__rmodal-stars" role="group" aria-label="Choose a star rating to start your review">
          {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="theinmag-reviews__rmodal-star"
              data-theinmag-rmodal-star
              data-rating="{{ i }}"
              aria-label="{{ i }} star{% if i > 1 %}s{% endif %}"
            >
              <span class="theinmag-reviews__star"></span>
            </button>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>

        <a
          class="theinmag-reviews__rmodal-go"
          data-theinmag-rmodal-go
          href="{{ store_review_link }}"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >{{ rmodal_cta | default: 'Write my review' }}</a>

        {%- if rmodal_note != blank -%}
          <p class="theinmag-reviews__rmodal-note">{{ rmodal_note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>

<script>
  /* Reparent Judge.me's featured_carousel items into the grid host so CSS columns can lay them out; cap the count + strip the carousel chrome. Mirrors the proven single-mags-hero port; re-runs on load in case Judge.me's app embed rearranges the markup after first paint. */
  (function () {
    function reparent(host) {
      var items = host.querySelectorAll('.jdgm-carousel-item');
      Array.prototype.forEach.call(items, function (item) {
        if (item.parentNode !== host) host.appendChild(item);
      });
      var cruft = host.querySelectorAll('.jdgm-carousel, .jdgm-carousel__items, .jdgm-carousel__item-container, .jdgm-carousel-title-and-link, .jdgm-carousel-title, .jdgm-carousel__arrows, .jdgm-carousel__arrow-left, .jdgm-carousel__arrow-right, .jdgm-carousel-number-of-reviews');
      Array.prototype.forEach.call(cruft, function (c) {
        if (c.parentNode) c.parentNode.removeChild(c);
      });
    }
    function initOne(root) {
      var host = root.querySelector('[data-theinmag-reviews-jdgm-host]');
      if (!host) return;
      reparent(host);
      var cap = parseInt(root.getAttribute('data-card-cap'), 10) || 4;
      var items = Array.prototype.slice.call(host.querySelectorAll('.jdgm-carousel-item'));
      if (!items.length) return;
      items.slice(cap).forEach(function (n) { if (n.parentNode) n.parentNode.removeChild(n); });
      root.classList.add('is-ready');
    }
    function init() {
      Array.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-theinmag-reviews-jdgm]'), initOne);
    }
    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
    } else {
      init();
    }
    window.addEventListener('load', function () { setTimeout(init, 50); });
  })();
</script>

<script>
  /* Review-invite bridge modal. The hosted Judge.me store-review form
     can't be iframed (x-frame-options: SAMEORIGIN), so this branded
     modal opens it in a new tab with the tapped rating pre-filled via a
     &rating=N param appended to the locked store-review link. */
  (function () {
    var modal = document.querySelector('[data-theinmag-rmodal]');
    if (!modal) return;

    var openers = document.querySelectorAll('[data-theinmag-rmodal-open]');
    var closers = modal.querySelectorAll('[data-theinmag-rmodal-close]');
    var stars = Array.prototype.slice.call(modal.querySelectorAll('[data-theinmag-rmodal-star]'));
    var goLink = modal.querySelector('[data-theinmag-rmodal-go]');
    var panel = modal.querySelector('.theinmag-reviews__rmodal-panel');
    var baseLink = modal.getAttribute('data-store-review-link') || (goLink && goLink.getAttribute('href')) || '';
    var lastOpener = null;

    function linkFor(rating) {
      if (!rating) return baseLink;
      var sep = baseLink.indexOf('?') === -1 ? '?' : '&';
      return baseLink + sep + 'rating=' + rating;
    }

    function paint(n) {
      stars.forEach(function (s, idx) { s.classList.toggle('is-on', idx < n); });
    }

    function openModal(opener) {
      lastOpener = opener || null;
      modal.hidden = false;
      modal.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');
      document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
      // Reflow before adding the class so the CSS transition runs.
      void modal.offsetWidth;
      modal.classList.add('is-open');
      paint(0);
      if (stars[0]) stars[0].focus();
    }

    function closeModal() {
      modal.classList.remove('is-open');
      modal.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
      document.body.style.overflow = '';
      window.setTimeout(function () { modal.hidden = true; }, 200);
      if (lastOpener && typeof lastOpener.focus === 'function') lastOpener.focus();
    }

    Array.prototype.forEach.call(openers, function (btn) {
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () { openModal(btn); });
    });
    Array.prototype.forEach.call(closers, function (btn) {
      btn.addEventListener('click', closeModal);
    });

    stars.forEach(function (star) {
      var rating = parseInt(star.getAttribute('data-rating'), 10) || 0;
      star.addEventListener('mouseenter', function () { paint(rating); });
      star.addEventListener('focus', function () { paint(rating); });
      star.addEventListener('click', function () {
        window.open(linkFor(rating), '_blank', 'noopener');
        closeModal();
      });
    });

    var starWrap = modal.querySelector('.theinmag-reviews__rmodal-stars');
    if (starWrap) starWrap.addEventListener('mouseleave', function () { paint(0); });

    // The plain "Write my review" button uses the base link (no rating).
    if (goLink) {
      goLink.addEventListener('click', function () {
        window.setTimeout(closeModal, 10);
      });
    }

    document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
      if (modal.hidden) return;
      if (e.key === 'Escape') { closeModal(); return; }
      // Simple focus trap inside the panel.
      if (e.key === 'Tab' && panel) {
        var focusable = panel.querySelectorAll('button, a[href], [tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])');
        if (!focusable.length) return;
        var first = focusable[0];
        var last = focusable[focusable.length - 1];
        if (e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first) { e.preventDefault(); last.focus(); }
        else if (!e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === last) { e.preventDefault(); first.focus(); }
      }
    });
  })();
</script>

{%- stylesheet -%}
  /* ================================================================
     theinmag-reviews
     Lavender section background extending the philosophy + meet-tam
     purple field downward - the three sections read as one continuous
     purple stretch, broken only by the cream cards on top. No cream
     panel wrapper. Cards float directly on the lavender.
     ================================================================ */

  .theinmag-reviews {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-color: #C9B5DB;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    padding: var(--reviews-pt, 64px) clamp(16px, 3vw, 32px) var(--reviews-pb, 64px);
    /* No negative margin - it was causing meet-tam's card shadow to
       get visually clipped where reviews' lavender layer started,
       creating a hard horizontal line. Both sections share the same
       lavender so the boundary is invisible without it. */
  }

  /* Optional painterly background swap if Tam paints one later. */
  .theinmag-reviews--has-bg {
    background-image: var(--reviews-bg);
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
  }

  /* Inner is a tighter centered container - cards stay compact and
     visibly centered within the viewport. position:relative + z-index
     keeps cards stacked above the dots pattern layer behind. */
  .theinmag-reviews__inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 920px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Decorative dots layer - anchored so the IMAGE'S CENTER sits at
     this section's TOP edge. Half the image is visible inside
     reviews (extending down from the boundary), half is above the
     boundary in meet-tam's space (clipped by overflow:hidden).

     The matching meet-tam dots layer mirrors this: its image center
     sits at meet-tam's BOTTOM edge with half visible above the
     boundary. Both halves come from the same image at the same
     horizontal position, so the pattern flows continuously across
     the section boundary - no visible seam.
     ================================================================ */
  .theinmag-reviews__dots {
    /* Hidden on mobile - the trail image stretches awkwardly at narrow
       widths. Desktop only. */
    display: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    .theinmag-reviews__dots {
      display: block;
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 50%;
      width: auto;
      height: auto;
      min-width: 220vw;
      min-height: 500vh;
      max-width: none;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(90deg);
      opacity: 0.32;
      pointer-events: none;
      z-index: 0;
      user-select: none;
    }
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Header row - heading + subhead on the left, aggregate rating on
     the right. Stacks vertically on narrow viewports.
     ================================================================ */

  .theinmag-reviews__header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: clamp(14px, 2vw, 22px);
    margin-bottom: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
    /* Mirror the blog-feed indent so the heading doesn't sit flush
       against the panel's left/right corners. */
    padding: 0 clamp(0px, 2vw, 32px);
  }

  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-reviews__header {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: var(--space-md, 16px);
    }
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__title-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(4px, 0.6vw, 8px);
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__heading {
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4.4vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__subhead {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(13px, 1.3vw, 15px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    opacity: 0.7;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Aggregate row - five stars, then optional "X.X - N reviews" once
     the count crosses the threshold. Below threshold (default 100)
     only the stars show. At zero the whole row is hidden in Liquid.
     ================================================================ */

  .theinmag-reviews__aggregate {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(8px, 1.2vw, 14px);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__stars {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3px;
  }

  /* Star primitive - SVG mask draws the shape, the element itself is
     the empty/grey base, ::after paints yellow over the masked shape
     and a clip-path controls the per-star fill (lets the aggregate
     show fractional ratings like 4.7 cleanly). */
  .theinmag-reviews__star {
    --star-mask: url("data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M12 2L9.19 8.62 2 9.27l5.46 4.73L5.82 21 12 17.27 18.18 21l-1.64-7L22 9.27l-7.19-.65z'/></svg>");
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    flex: 0 0 22px;
    background-color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.18);
    -webkit-mask-image: var(--star-mask);
            mask-image: var(--star-mask);
    -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat;
            mask-repeat: no-repeat;
    -webkit-mask-position: center;
            mask-position: center;
    -webkit-mask-size: contain;
            mask-size: contain;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__star::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-color: var(--color-yellow, #F9C23C);
    clip-path: inset(0 calc(100% - var(--fill, 100%)) 0 0);
  }

  /* Card stars - small to keep cards compact. */
  .theinmag-reviews__card-stars .theinmag-reviews__star {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    flex: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__aggregate-text {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(14px, 1.4vw, 16px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__aggregate-value {
    color: var(--color-cherry, #B8265E);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__aggregate-sep {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /* Judge.me hydrated mode - the App Embed JS injects content after
     load. Container styled to match the manual mode so the layout
     doesn't shift when JS finishes. */
  .theinmag-reviews__aggregate-jdgm {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(14px, 1.4vw, 16px);
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(8px, 1.2vw, 14px);
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Layout: two-column on desktop. Left = stacked text cards.
     Right = single video card with body below. Mobile stacks all
     three cards (video first because it's the headline content).
     ================================================================ */

  .theinmag-reviews__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 16px);
  }

  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-reviews__layout {
      /* Text column wider, video column narrower - cuts the video
         card's overall height (smaller square, smaller card) so the
         whole section fits in one viewport. */
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.7fr;
      gap: clamp(16px, 1.6vw, 20px);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  /* Left column - stack of text-only review cards. Mobile: appears
     below the video (order:2). Desktop: left column. */
  .theinmag-reviews__text-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 16px);
    order: 2;
  }

  /* Right column - the single video card. */
  .theinmag-reviews__video-column {
    position: relative;
    order: 1;
    display: flex;
  }

  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-reviews__text-stack {
      order: unset;
      grid-column: 1;
    }
    .theinmag-reviews__video-column {
      order: unset;
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }

  /* Sharp-cornered cream tiles floating on the lavender. Subtle
     shadow lifts each tile off the purple. */
  .theinmag-reviews__card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background-color: var(--color-cream, #FBF6EA);
    border-radius: 0;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 18px rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.14);
    transition: transform var(--transition-hover, 0.2s ease), box-shadow var(--transition-hover, 0.2s ease);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Text-only cards in the left stack: content-sized (no flex:1) so
     the card snugs to its body length instead of stretching to match
     the video card. */
  .theinmag-reviews__card--text {
    padding: clamp(14px, 1.4vw, 18px);
    gap: clamp(8px, 0.9vw, 10px);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__card--video {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__card-video-body {
    padding: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 16px) clamp(14px, 1.4vw, 18px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(6px, 0.8vw, 8px);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__card-stars {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3px;
  }

  /* Video frame - flush to the card edges. 1:1 square keeps the
     overall section short enough to fit in a single viewport while
     still giving the video real presence. */
  .theinmag-reviews__card-video {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.08);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__card-video video {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__card-body {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1vw, 13.5px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }

  /* Attribution - name + location stacked. mt:auto pushes it to the
     bottom of the card so the line aligns even when bodies differ
     in length. Photo avatars are not rendered on the homepage; the
     schema field stays for use on /pages/reviews later. */
  .theinmag-reviews__card-attribution {
    margin: auto 0 0;
    padding-top: clamp(6px, 0.7vw, 8px);
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__card-name {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__card-location {
    font-weight: 400;
    opacity: 0.7;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Read-all CTA - outlined dark teal pill, mirrors the blog feed's
     see-all button so the two sections share a button language.
     ================================================================ */

  /* CTA sits inside the text-stack column, centered horizontally
     within the column width. Small top margin gives breathing room
     from the card above. */
  .theinmag-reviews__cta-wrap {
    margin: clamp(4px, 0.6vw, 8px) 0 0;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: transparent;
    color: var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A);
    border-radius: 32px;
    padding: 8px 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease;
    min-height: 36px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__cta:hover,
  .theinmag-reviews__cta:focus-visible {
    background-color: var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A);
    color: #FFFFFF;
    outline: none;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Judge.me masonry - featured_carousel items reparented into a
     CSS-columns mosaic, restyled as cream cards. The position / opacity
     / transform / display overrides are load-bearing: Judge.me's own
     carousel CSS stacks all but the active item off-screen, so without
     them only one card would show.
     ================================================================ */

  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding: 0 clamp(0px, 2vw, 32px);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid {
    column-count: 1;
    column-gap: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 16px);
  }

  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid {
      column-count: 2;
      column-gap: clamp(16px, 1.6vw, 20px);
    }
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item {
    display: flex !important;
    flex-direction: column;
    position: static !important;
    transform: none !important;
    opacity: 1 !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    max-width: 100% !important;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0 0 clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 16px) !important;
    padding: clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 20px) !important;
    background-color: var(--color-cream, #FBF6EA) !important;
    border: 0 !important;
    border-radius: 0 !important;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 18px rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.14) !important;
    break-inside: avoid;
    -webkit-column-break-inside: avoid;
    page-break-inside: avoid;
  }

  /* Field order inside each card: stars -> title -> body -> name -> date. */
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__review-rating { order: 1; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__review-title { order: 2; }
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__review-body { order: 3; }
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__reviewer-name { order: 4; }
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__timestamp { order: 5; }

  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__review-rating .jdgm-star {
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-star.jdgm--on { color: var(--color-yellow, #F9C23C) !important; }
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-star.jdgm--off { color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.18) !important; }

  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__review-title {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(13px, 1.2vw, 15px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__review-body {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1vw, 13.5px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__reviewer-name {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    margin: 10px 0 0;
  }
  /* Drop Judge.me's carousel chrome + per-item product link, timestamp
     (ships as an empty spinner in the static metafield), verified badge,
     and any empty title. We strip Judge.me's own <style> block when
     reparenting, so these must be hidden here rather than relying on its
     injected display:none rules. */
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-title-and-link,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-title,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-number-of-reviews,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel__arrows,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel__left-arrow,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel__right-arrow,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__product,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__product-title,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__product-info,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__product-image,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__timestamp,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__verified-badge,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__reviewer-verified,
  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-spinner {
    display: none !important;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__jdgm-grid .jdgm-carousel-item__review-title:empty {
    display: none;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__cta-wrap--jdgm {
    margin-top: clamp(16px, 2vw, 24px);
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Random kid character - slides in horizontally from off-screen
     LEFT, fills the empty lavender gap between the section's left
     edge and the inner container. Only shows at >=1200px viewport
     where there's actually room for it. Hidden on tablet/mobile.
     ================================================================ */

  .theinmag-reviews__character {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1200px) {
    .theinmag-reviews__character {
      display: block;
      position: absolute;
      left: clamp(0px, 1.5vw, 24px);
      top: 50%;
      width: clamp(140px, 14vw, 220px);
      pointer-events: none;
      z-index: 0;
      /* Initial state: fully off-screen to the left. Translate uses
         vertical -50% to center the character against the section's
         vertical midpoint. */
      transform: translate(-130%, -50%);
      transition: transform 0.85s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.4, 0.64, 1);
    }

    .theinmag-reviews__character.is-popped {
      transform: translate(0, -50%);
      animation: theinmag-reviews-bob 4s ease-in-out infinite 0.9s;
    }
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__character-img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* Sitewide pool snippet adds .theinmag-pool-character__img with its
     own bob. Reviews already animates the wrapper (slide-in + bob), so
     we silence the pool's img-level bob here. */
  .theinmag-reviews__character .theinmag-pool-character__img {
    animation: none;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* Bob keyframes preserve the -50% Y translate so the bob layers on
     top of the slide-in's final position without resetting it. */
  @keyframes theinmag-reviews-bob {
    0%, 100% { transform: translate(0, -50%) rotate(-2deg); }
    50%      { transform: translate(0, calc(-50% - 6px)) rotate(2deg); }
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Reduced motion - skip the slide-in and the bob.
     ================================================================ */

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .theinmag-reviews__card,
    .theinmag-reviews__cta,
    .theinmag-reviews__character {
      transition: none;
      animation: none;
    }
    .theinmag-reviews__card-wrap:hover .theinmag-reviews__card,
    .theinmag-reviews__card-wrap:focus-within .theinmag-reviews__card {
      transform: none;
    }
    @media (min-width: 1200px) {
      .theinmag-reviews__character,
      .theinmag-reviews__character.is-popped {
        transform: translate(0, -50%);
        animation: none;
      }
    }
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Review invite - the clickable bridge band above the cards. Cream
     tile matching the review cards so it reads as part of the set, but
     with a yellow stamp CTA marking it as the one interactive prompt.
     ================================================================ */

  .theinmag-reviews__invite {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding: 0 clamp(0px, 2vw, 32px);
    margin-bottom: clamp(16px, 2.4vw, 28px);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__invite-card {
    appearance: none;
    width: 100%;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-align: left;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(10px, 1.6vw, 18px);
    background-color: var(--color-cream, #FBF6EA);
    border: 1px dashed rgba(93, 58, 122, 0.45);
    border-radius: 0;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 18px rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.14);
    padding: clamp(14px, 1.8vw, 20px) clamp(16px, 2vw, 24px);
    transition: transform var(--transition-hover, 0.2s ease), box-shadow var(--transition-hover, 0.2s ease), border-color var(--transition-hover, 0.2s ease);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__invite-card:hover,
  .theinmag-reviews__invite-card:focus-visible {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 26px rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.2);
    border-color: var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A);
    outline: none;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__invite-card:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__invite-stars {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2px;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__invite-stars .theinmag-reviews__star {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    flex: 0 0 16px;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__invite-copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    min-width: 0;
    flex: 1 1 240px;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__invite-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.5vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__invite-text {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(12.5px, 1.2vw, 14px);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    opacity: 0.78;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__invite-cta {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    background-color: var(--color-yellow, #F9C23C);
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    border-radius: 32px;
    padding: 9px 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__invite-cta::after {
    content: '\2192';
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     Review-invite modal (bridge to the Judge.me store-review form).
     ================================================================ */

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 999;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: clamp(16px, 4vw, 32px);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-backdrop {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.55);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal.is-open .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-backdrop {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-panel {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 460px;
    background-color: var(--color-cream, #FBF6EA);
    border-radius: 14px;
    box-shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.4);
    padding: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px) clamp(22px, 3vw, 36px) clamp(24px, 3vw, 32px);
    text-align: center;
    transform: translateY(12px) scale(0.98);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: transform 0.24s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.4, 0.64, 1), opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal.is-open .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-panel {
    transform: translateY(0) scale(1);
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-x {
    position: absolute;
    top: 12px;
    right: 12px;
    appearance: none;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 8px;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    opacity: 0.6;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
    line-height: 0;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-x:hover,
  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-x:focus-visible {
    opacity: 1;
    outline: none;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 3.2vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-body {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(13.5px, 1.4vw, 15px);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    opacity: 0.8;
    margin: 0 auto clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 24px);
    max-width: 34ch;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-stars {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: clamp(6px, 1.2vw, 10px);
    margin-bottom: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 24px);
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-star {
    appearance: none;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 4px;
    cursor: pointer;
    line-height: 0;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-star:hover,
  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-star:focus-visible {
    transform: scale(1.12);
    outline: none;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-star .theinmag-reviews__star {
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    flex: 0 0 34px;
    --fill: 0%;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-star.is-on .theinmag-reviews__star {
    --fill: 100%;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-go {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: var(--color-yellow, #F9C23C);
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    border-radius: 32px;
    padding: 11px 28px;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-go:hover,
  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-go:focus-visible {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(249, 194, 60, 0.5);
    outline: none;
  }

  .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-note {
    margin: clamp(12px, 1.6vw, 16px) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .theinmag-reviews__invite-card,
    .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-backdrop,
    .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-panel,
    .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-star,
    .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-go {
      transition: none;
    }
    .theinmag-reviews__rmodal-panel {
      transform: none;
    }
  }
{%- endstylesheet -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Per-section character handling (image pick + scroll-pop) was removed
  in the May 10 2026 sitewide retrofit. The sitewide character-pool
  snippet (rendered above) handles both the image fill and the
  scroll-triggered .is-popped class.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "theINmag reviews",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "theinmag-reviews-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "What are families saying?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subhead",
      "label": "Subhead (optional)"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Aggregate rating"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Manual mode below is fine for launch. The threshold keeps the section honest while reviews are being collected - below the threshold only stars show, no inflated number. Flip 'Auto-pull from Judge.me' on once enough reviews are flowing in to trust the live feed."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "use_judgeme_widget",
      "label": "Auto-pull from Judge.me",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Uses the Judge.me JS-hydrated widget for live count + rating. Leave off for now."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "aggregate_rating",
      "label": "Manual rating",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 5,
      "step": 0.1,
      "default": 5,
      "unit": "★"
    },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "review_count",
      "label": "Manual review count",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "Set to zero before launch to hide the aggregate row entirely."
    },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "show_count_threshold",
      "label": "Show count from this many reviews",
      "default": 100,
      "info": "Below this number only stars show. Once you have this many reviews, the rating value and count appear too."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Review cards"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When on, the cards pull live from your Judge.me featured carousel - mark reviews as 'featured' in Judge.me to choose which ones show. When off, or before any reviews are featured, the manual review blocks are shown instead."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "use_judgeme_cards",
